[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Document" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/core/document.gd" id="1_doc"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_doc")
id = &"d09a_operating_card"
title = "Standby set — operating instructions"
byline = "printed card, taped inside the transfer switch cabinet door"
hand = 3
body = "ONAN 30 KW STANDBY SET
MANUAL TRANSFER — OPERATING SEQUENCE

TO EXERCISE THE SET (MONTHLY, NO LOAD)

1  OPEN DAY TANK ISOLATING VALVE
2  SELECTOR TO TEST
3  PRESS START. ENGINE RUNS UNLOADED.
4  RUN 30 MINUTES MINIMUM
5  PRESS STOP. SELECTOR TO NORMAL.
6  CLOSE DAY TANK ISOLATING VALVE

TO CARRY LOAD ON LOSS OF STATION SERVICE

1  OPEN DAY TANK ISOLATING VALVE
2  PRESS START. ALLOW TO COME UP TO SPEED.
3  SELECTOR TO EMERGENCY
4  CLOSE SET MAIN

CAUTION

THE SET WILL NOT CARRY THE STATION. SHED LOAD
AT THE DISTRIBUTION PANEL BEFORE CLOSING THE
SET MAIN. SEE NAMEPLATE RATINGS.

IN TEST THE ENGINE RUNS BUT IS NOT CONNECTED.

FORM 928-B"
